@startuml sequence-application-submit
' Preparing, approving and submitting an application, as a sequence.
'
' The decision is the gate. The approval record holds the exact payload that
' was reviewed, and that stored payload is what is submitted, so what a person
' approved is what the employer receives.

!include _style.puml

actor "Candidate" as Person
participant "REST API" as API
participant "Application graph" as Graph
database "Approval store" as Approvals
participant "Application adapter" as Adapter
participant "Evidence" as Evidence

Person -> API : POST /api/applications/prepare
API -> Approvals : write the approval request
Approvals --> API : approval_id
API --> Person : the payload to review

note over Person, API : nothing is submitted until a person decides

Person -> API : POST .../approve
API -> Graph : execute_approved()
Graph -> Graph : the approval node reads the decision
alt approved
  Graph -> Adapter : submit(stored payload)
  Adapter -> Evidence : screenshot, trace, confirmation text
  Evidence --> Graph : evidence
  Graph -> Approvals : move to SUBMITTED
  Graph --> API : status and evidence
else rejected
  Graph -> Approvals : move to REJECTED
  Graph --> API : status
end
API --> Person : the result

@enduml
